#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:3
msgid "JSON output"
msgstr "JSON 輸出"

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:5
msgid ""
"Most pipx commands accept ``--output json`` to print a single machine-"
"readable result envelope on stdout instead of human-readable text. Selecting "
"JSON suppresses pipx's own progress messages and sends whatever pip or uv "
"print while installing to stderr, so the envelope is the only thing on "
"stdout. When ``install`` moves to another Python because the package's "
"``requires-python`` rules out the default one, pipx says so on stderr as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:12
msgid "Envelope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:14
msgid ""
"The envelope is a JSON object with these keys (serialized with sorted keys):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:20
msgid "Key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:21
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:22
msgid "``pipx_result_version``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:23
msgid "Envelope schema version, currently ``\"1\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:24
msgid "``command``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:25
msgid ""
"The command tokens as a list, for example ``[\"install\"]`` or ``[\"cache\", "
"\"dir\"]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:26
msgid "``status``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:27
msgid ""
"``\"success\"`` when there are no errors, ``\"partial\"`` when the run both "
"succeeded somewhere and recorded errors, ``\"error\"`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:29
msgid "``exit_code``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:30
msgid "The integer process exit code (see :doc:`exit-codes`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:31
msgid "``data``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:32
msgid "Command-specific payload object. Its fields depend on the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:33
msgid "``errors``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:34
msgid ""
"List of error objects. Each has ``code``, ``message``, and the optional "
"identity fields ``environment`` and ``package``. When pip or uv fails an "
"``install``, its ``message`` ends with the installer's error output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:37
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"pipx_result_version\": \"1\",\n"
"  \"command\": [\"install\"],\n"
"  \"status\": \"success\",\n"
"  \"exit_code\": 0,\n"
"  \"data\": {},\n"
"  \"errors\": []\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"{\n"
"  \"pipx_result_version\": \"1\",\n"
"  \"command\": [\"install\"],\n"
"  \"status\": \"success\",\n"
"  \"exit_code\": 0,\n"
"  \"data\": {},\n"
"  \"errors\": []\n"
"}"

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:48
msgid ""
"Once the arguments parse, a failure on a JSON-enabled command still speaks "
"the envelope. That covers an invalid environment variable such as "
"``PIPX_COOLDOWN``, a ``--python`` that cannot be resolved, a path or URL "
"where a package name belongs, and ``--backend uv`` without a ``uv`` "
"executable. The envelope has a ``status`` of ``\"error\"`` and a single "
"error whose ``code`` is ``pipx_error``, and pipx exits ``1``. Only argument-"
"parsing errors, such as an unknown option or a missing argument, print plain "
"text instead: the usage message goes to stderr and pipx exits ``2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:56
msgid "Supported commands"
msgstr "支援的命令"

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:58
msgid ""
"``--output json`` is available on: ``install``, ``inject``, ``uninject``, "
"``expose``, ``unexpose``, ``pin``, ``unpin``, ``upgrade``, ``upgrade-all``, "
"``upgrade-shared``, ``uninstall``, ``uninstall-all``, ``reinstall``, "
"``reinstall-all``, ``reset``, ``health``, ``repair``, ``manifest lock``, "
"``manifest sync``, ``interpreter list``, ``interpreter prune``, "
"``interpreter upgrade``, ``cache dir``, ``cache purge``, and ``list --"
"outdated``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:63
msgid ""
"It is not available on ``install-all``, ``run``, ``exec``, ``runpip``, "
"``ensurepath``, ``environment``, ``completions``, or ``help``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:68
msgid "``list`` is different"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:70
msgid ""
"``pipx list --output json`` without ``--outdated`` does not emit the result "
"envelope; errors still use it. It prints the installed-package snapshot that "
"``install-all`` reads back: an object with ``pipx_spec_version`` (currently "
"``\"0.1\"``) and a ``venvs`` map of environment name to an object whose "
"``metadata`` key holds that environment's metadata (see :doc:`metadata`). "
"``pipx list --json`` is a legacy alias for the same snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:75
msgid ""
"$ pipx list --output json > pipx.json\n"
"$ pipx install-all pipx.json"
msgstr ""
"$ pipx list --output json > pipx.json\n"
"$ pipx install-all pipx.json"

#: ../../../reference/json-output.rst:80
msgid ""
"``--json`` is a legacy alias only on ``list``; every other command uses ``--"
"output json``."
msgstr ""
